      "side": 1,
      "message": "Also, fwiw, I think we should keep open the possibility of allowing an arbitrary API to provide stubs as an orthogonal mechanism. The core problem is that when we have stubs, we automatically start using the library as llndk. This isn\u0027t right, we should continue to use it as a vndk library w/ stubs and have some separate indication that a library is in the llndk. So, I\u0027m assuming that this current CL is just a stopgap for now?",
